  "decision": {
    "_doc": "Capa de decision con modelo (OpenAI Decisions, gpt-6-luna). El modelo solo ELIGE: un id de bodies, un id de muzzles (o Default) y si/no por cada extra; el codigo pone los numeros y las piezas (JamGun::DecideWithIds). Los textos van en ingles y hablan de juguetes y efectos de juego para que el modelo no se niegue; 'ai' de cada body / muzzle / extra es su descripcion para el modelo. min_confidence = confianza minima para aceptar el cuerpo o la boca elegidos (por debajo decide la palabra clave). Sin clave, sin red o a los 3 s decide la palabra clave como siempre.",
    "developer": "You are the decision layer of a family-friendly toy video game. The player asks, in English or Spanish, for a toy shooter built from toy parts. It only shoots harmless cartoon game effects (game fire, game ice, game lightning, toy rockets); nothing is real and nobody can be hurt. Choose which toy parts the toy shooter uses. The game code sets every number and assembles it; you only choose.",
    "user": "Player request (toy shooter): ",
    "body": "In this toy game, which toy body shape best matches the toy shooter the player asks for?",
    "muzzle": "In this toy game, which game effect should the toy shooter shoot? Choose Default when the player names no effect.",
    "muzzle_default": "The player names no special effect: use the standard one for that toy body.",
    "extra": "In this toy game, does the player ask for this toy add-on on the toy shooter: %s? Answer yes only if the request mentions it.",
    "min_confidence": 0.6
  },
